   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 2.5",
   "body_html": "Similar question here: <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/1037575/why-arent-exceptions-in-c-checked-by-the-compiler\" title=\"why arent exceptions in c checked by the compiler\">stackoverflow.com/questions/1037575/&hellip;</a>"
  },
  {
   "post_type": "comment",
   "post_id": 1252380,
   "parent_id": 1410255,
   "parent_type": "answer",
   "author_user_id": 20972,
   "author_display_name": "Dominic Rodger",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": null,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/1410226/#comment1252380_1410255",
   "score": 0,
   "created_utc": "2009-09-11T11:01:26Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 2.5",
   "body_html": "That&#39;s my understanding too. Why you&#39;d want it to do so I&#39;ve no idea. I personally find <code>GetFoo() &#47;&#47; throws(std::runtime_error)</code> much more useful than the uncommented equivalent - just as a hint to consumers of my code."
  },
  {
   "post_type": "comment",
   "post_id": 1252383,
   "parent_id": 1410255,
   "parent_type": "answer",
   "author_user_id": 15416,
   "author_display_name": "MSalters",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": null,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/1410226/#comment1252383_1410255",
   "score": 1,
   "created_utc": "2009-09-11T11:02:13Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 2.5",
   "body_html": "Correct. The practical problem for compile-time checking is that most existing C++ code has no throw specification."
  },
  {
   "post_type": "answer",
   "post_id": 1410270,
   "parent_id": 1410226,
   "author_user_id": 140719,
   "author_display_name": "sbi",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/1410270",
   "score": 2,
   "created_utc": "2009-09-11T11:02:59Z",
   "last_edit_utc": "2017-05-23T12:04:24Z",
   "last_activity_utc": "2009-09-11T13:33:58Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<p>Basically, the exception specifications are only good as empty exception specification. Otherwise I think they're an experiment that failed. See <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/1410226/is-there-any-use-for-c-throw-decoration/1410294#1410294\">phlipsy's answer</a> why. </p>\n"
  },
  {
   "post_type": "comment",
   "post_id": 1252397,
   "parent_id": 1410255,
   "parent_type": "answer",
   "author_user_id": 123111,
   "author_display_name": "Kirill V. Lyadvinsky",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": null,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/1410226/#comment1252397_1410255",
   "score": 8,
   "created_utc": "2009-09-11T11:05:50Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 2.5",
   "body_html": "Visual C++ 2008 doesn&#39;t support this part of standard."
  },
  {
   "post_type": "answer",
   "post_id": 1410294,
   "parent_id": 1410226,
   "author_user_id": 71051,
   "author_display_name": "phlipsy",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/1410294",
   "score": 8,
   "created_utc": "2009-09-11T11:12:00Z",
   "last_edit_utc": null,
   "last_activity_utc": "2009-09-11T11:12:00Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 2.5",
   "body_html": "<p>I would also recommend to look at <a href=\"http://www.gotw.ca/publications/mill22.htm\" rel=\"noreferrer\">this</a> essay about the exception specifications. It points out the problems of this C++ feature like:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>It's a shadow type system</li>\n<li>The compiler checks thrown exceptions only at runtime</li>\n<li>The triggered default behavior in the case of a thrown but not specified exception is usually unusable and often misunderstood by the programmers</li>\n</ul>\n"
  },
